.TH GM-GATHER 1 “2025-11-21” “gm-tools” “User Commands”
.SH NAME
gm-gather \- Utility to gather files from remote hosts to local
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gm-gather
\fR[\-h|\-\-help] [\-H|\-\-hosts \fIFILE\fR] [\-u|\-\-user \fIUSER\fR] [\-s|\-\-ssh-user \fIUSER\fR]
.br
\fR[\-P|\-\-port \fIPORT\fR] [\-K|\-\-key \fIPATH\fR] [\-W|\-\-password \fIPASS\fR] [\-T|\-\-timeout \fISEC\fR]
.br
\fR[\-S|\-\-strict-host-key-checking] [\-j|\-\-parallel \fIN\fR] [\-n|\-\-dry-run] [\-v|\-\-verbose]
.br
\fR[\-\-pack] [\-\-follow-symlinks] [\-x|\-\-sudo-collect|\-\-no-sudo-collect]
.br
\fRSRC... DEST
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgm-gather\fR collects regular files from multiple remote hosts listed in the host list and saves them to the specified local directory. It supports two transfer methods: sequential transfer using SSH/SFTP, and pack processing, which creates temporary archives per host for download. Logs are output in structured key=value format, allowing tracking of collected items and warning/error counts.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBSRC...\fR
Specifies one or more retrieval patterns. Details on literals, regular expressions, and tilde expansion are in the “Path and Regular Expression Specifications”. Invalid patterns are excluded from collection.
.TP
\fBDEST\fR
The local output directory. Relative paths are converted to absolute paths relative to the current directory at execution time. `~` or `~user` formats will cause an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Connection and Authentication
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-hosts\fR \fIFILE\fR
Specifies a host file listing the target hosts for operations. By default, it reads \fBhostfile\fR in the current directory.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
The username to collect data for. Used for `~/` expansion in `SRC` and permission checks; defaults to the command execution user.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-ssh-user\fR \fIUSER\fR
The username used for SSH login. If omitted, it defaults to the same as `\fB\-\-user\fR` and is used to determine whether to automatically use sudo.
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
The SSH port number. Default is 22.
.TP
\fB\-K\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fIPATH\fR
SSH private key file. If unspecified, known keys under $HOME/.ssh/ are tried sequentially; if the SSH agent is enabled, registered keys are also used. Explicitly specify the key path to ensure public key authentication is used.
.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fIPASS\fR
SSH password. Key-based authentication is recommended as passwords are logged in the shell history.
.SS Execution Control
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR
SSH session and remote command timeout in seconds. Default is 30 seconds; uses the same value from home directory detection to archive deletion.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-strict-host-key-checking\fR
Rejects unknown host keys and does not connect to hosts not in known_hosts. If omitted, automatically registers unknown keys.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-parallel\fR \fIN\fR
Number of parallel processes per host. Values less than 1 are rounded up to 1. Default is 4. Processing within each host is executed sequentially.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry-run\fR
Performs only collection plan construction and item count aggregation; does not perform transfers. Exit code is always 0.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enables additional debug logging. Also applies during dry-run mode.
.SS Transfer Method
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR
Creates temporary tar.gz files on the remote host per host and extracts them all at once in a single download. If omitted, performs sequential transfer using SFTP.
.TP
\fB\-\-follow-symlinks\fR
\fB\-\-pack\fR When used, follows symbolic links and collects the actual files at the link destinations. Always excludes links in SFTP mode.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-sudo-collect\fR
Always performs file enumeration and tar/gzip execution on pack paths using `sudo -n`.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-sudo-collect\fR
Does not use sudo on the pack path. If both options are omitted, `sudo -n` is automatically enabled only when the SSH login user differs from the target user.
.SH TRANSFER MODES
.SS SFTP Sequential Transfer
.PP
Calls SFTP `get` for each collection target. Directories are included in the target list but their contents are not transferred. Local destination directories are created as needed. Complete metadata restoration is not guaranteed.
.SS Pack Transfer
.PP
Creates a tar.gz per host and extracts it after download. Detects available tar commands; if `--follow-symlinks` is enabled and supported, symbolic links are treated as regular files. During extraction, path traversal is rejected; if the parent directory is a symbolic link, the item is skipped. GNU tar hard link information is restored as regular files.
.SS Target Differences
.TP
Regular Files
SFTP retrieves only those identified as regular files. Pack mode restores regular files and hard links contained within the archive.
.TP
Directories
SFTP includes them in the target list but does not transfer their contents. Pack mode recreates them during extraction, skipping if the parent directory is a symbolic link.
.TP
Symbolic Links
Always excluded by SFTP. Pack method only captures the link target when \fB\-\-follow-symlinks\fR is specified; if it fails, the link itself is excluded.
.TP
Device/FIFO/Socket
Excluded during enumeration by SFTP; excluded during safety checks at extraction by the pack method.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Normal exit, or when executing \fB\-\-dry-run\fR.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Could not obtain a valid host from the host file.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Hosts with transfer errors exist.
.TP
\fB3\fR
Specified a path containing `~user`.
.TP
\fB4\fR
Insufficient `SRC`/`DEST`, or specified `~` alone.
.SH SIGNALS
.PP
Upon receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM, does not start new host processing and notifies ongoing hosts of cancellation. After interruption, outputs warning log “Interrupt requested; cancelling remaining transfers…” and returns exit code 0 or 2 based on completion status. The termination process closes open sessions and deletes temporary directories.
.SH LOGGING
.PP
Logs output fixed keys `timestamp`, `level`, `host`, `op`, `phase`, `trial`, `processed`, `total`, followed by optional keys like `warnings`, `errors`, `duration`, `seq` in key=value format. `phase` uses `start`, `processing`, `done`. Aggregate lines append `host=-` and `msg=summary`.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
gm-gather specification (docs/gm-gather-spec.md), gm-scatter(1)
